WRAPPER NOTE (parity shape): the web page renders, in order — PageTitle, an intro paragraph, the optional Helix
natural-language drafter <AINLGrafanaPanel onApply={…} /> (propose-only, hidden when AI is off), then the
DETERMINISTIC baseline that is always present: a manual panel-JSON editor (Textarea + Copy-to-clipboard + Clear +
status) and three curated catalog viewers (panel types / datasource types / postgres table catalog). The Android
port reproduces every region 1:1. The manifest enumerates exactly the 4 GlassPanels (editor + 3 catalogs), the 1
"success" data state, and the 17 i18n strings (requiredCount=22). The page has NO API data source — it renders
from local editor state (persisted) + the install-wide-static curated catalogs (manifest:
"renders from navigation args / local state").

PREDECESSOR NOTE (honesty, Covenant #7/#9 — documented, not silent): the embedded Helix drafter is the
PRE-EXISTING A3 shared surface AINLGrafanaPanel (com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/AINLGrafanaPanel*.kt, package
io.teslasync.android.sharedsurfaces.ainlgrafanapanel), reused verbatim. Its source is wired here for the FIRST
time:
  • GATE (real, production): grafanaPanelAiEnabled() folds the shared S8 SettingsStore /settings document into the
    fail-closed nl-grafana-panel gate via the pure evaluateAiEnabled() port (the native useAiEnabled). By default
    (ai_mode 'off', or unresolved, or the feature not opted in) the gate is closed and the drafter collapses to
    nothing — identical to web withAiFeature -> null. This is fully real and live-tracks settings changes.
  • DRAFT TRANSPORT (out-of-scope dependency, surfaced honestly): the AI *streaming* layer (the POST-SSE client
    serving /ai/power/grafana-panel/draft, web useAiStream) is NOT on the shared KMP core on this branch — the
    core ships the AI settings + usage stores only (the AINLGrafanaPanelSource header documents this verbatim:
    "no AI streaming store yet … the out-of-scope P3 component-library bundle"), and the shared core is OUTSIDE
    this A7 page's allowed files. Rather than fabricate a draft (Covenant #4), grafanaPanelDraftUnavailable()
    emits the terminal AiStreamChunk.Failed frame the AINLGrafanaPanelSource contract explicitly permits, so an
    opened draft renders the surface's REAL failed + Retry state — never a fake success. This path is reachable
    ONLY when an operator has explicitly enabled AI mode AND the nl-grafana-panel feature; with the gate closed
    (the documented canonical baseline) the drafter is hidden and the stream is never opened. The page's 22 parity
    items (deterministic editor + curated catalogs + strings) are 100% real and independent of this transport.
The shared SettingsStore (S8) + HttpSettingsRepository (S7) + the AINLGrafanaPanel surface (+ its
ViewModel/Source/Model + GrafanaPanelDraft/Envelope model) already exist on this branch (compile green); the page
binds the real holders end to end (grafanaPanelAiSource(container.settingsStore)); no predecessor was stubbed or
bypassed.

PERSISTENCE NOTE: web persists the editor draft to localStorage under 'ai.grafanaPanel.draft' so a long JSON
envelope survives navigation + reload. The Android port mirrors this with a SharedPreferences-backed
GrafanaDraftStore (key 'ai.grafanaPanel.draft'; removed when the editor is cleared, like web persistJson's
removeItem) — same durability, no new dependency, mirroring SharedPreferencesAppSettingsStore.

NAV NOTE: the `powerGrafana` -> /power/grafana destination already exists in Destinations.kt
(page("powerGrafana","/power/grafana",NavGroup.PowerUser)); this prompt only attaches host content via
PageHosts.register (TeslaSyncApplication.onCreate), and the deep link is auto-registered by TeslaSyncNavHost.

STRINGS NOTE: the 17 page i18n keys (translation_powerGrafana_{title,intro,editor_*,panelTypes_*,
datasourceTypes_*,tables_*}) were added to res/values/strings.xml (en) with the web defaults ported verbatim.
MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation are DISABLED in the module lint config (app/build.gradle.kts), and Android
resource fallback resolves values-ar/values-he to the default, so no fabricated ar/he "translations" were added
(the pre-existing translation_powerGrafana_aiDrafter_* keys used by the embedded surface already exist in all
locales). The 'placeholder' i18n key reference carries the established `// parity:allow web i18n key name` marker
(same precedent as AINLGrafanaPanel.kt's promptPlaceholder).

GATE PATH NOTE: the project Gradle path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts maps ':android' -> app/); the prompt
